{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_development", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "The incident involves a potential failure in safety-critical detection (CAV block) due to algorithmic disagreement between bedside and cloud logs.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1 requires devices to ensure reliability and reduce risks in case of fault conditions.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "The static analysis reports provided are relevant to the current incident.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "The test logs provided describe the same event type (CAV block) or environment.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}], "confidence": 0.58, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a 'discordance' between bedside and cloud logs regarding Complete Atrioventricular (CAV) block detection thresholds in the context of an irregularity reported by field service engineering. While no adverse outcome occurred, this represents a potential failure to detect or classify a safety-critical arrhythmia correctly due to algorithmic disagreement across environments. This aligns with EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1 requirements for repeatability and reliability in the event of fault conditions (mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable). However, the retrieved technical artifacts do not explicitly confirm this discordance or provide data on why the logs disagree; they instead describe confidence scores for a *missed ventricular tachycardia* episode from different releases, which is unrelated to the reported CAV block irregularity event.\n\nThe static analysis reports (ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A and ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2018A) are explicitly noted as being for 'unrelated firmware modules' and do not describe this specific field incident. The test logs (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A and ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A) concern a missed ventricular tachycardia episode, which is distinct from the reported CAV block irregularity; therefore, they cannot ground claims about the current discordance mechanism. This lack of direct technical evidence regarding the specific event limits confidence to 0.68 (slightly above threshold but low for definitive causality) and necessitates investigation into why the logs disagree before any corrective action can be taken.\n\nThe incident is not a confirmed life-threatening event with realized harm, keeping severity at Level 2 (moderate concern regarding detection reliability). It does not meet criteria for Field Safety Corrective Action as there is no evidence of recurrence or broad population exposure yet. Human review is required to investigate the root cause of the log discordance.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "2e86162ca5bfa0cc78f2ef016a52816b47ea1d097946ad4ec61d45b87dfa748e", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0017", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0017_r5", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0017", "schema_version": "